<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-09-30T16:23:56+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:23:56 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[NY man allegedly took brother’s Social Security after death; payments reached $109,746]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134587693.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[David Darling allegedly accessed his deceased brother's bank account to withdraw funds starting one day after his death. Social Security continued payments into the account, unaware of the brother's passing. Darling's actions reportedly led to $109,746 in stolen benefits, resulting in federal charges against him. The Justice Department's crackdown involved multiple cases of Social Security fraud across various states.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-york-man-allegedly-began-withdrawing-money-from-his-brothers-account-the-day-after-his-death-while-social-security-remained-unaware-he-had-died-prosecutors-say-the-continuing-payments-ultimately-reached-109746/articleshow/134587693.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-york-man-allegedly-began-withdrawing-money-from-his-brothers-account-the-day-after-his-death-while-social-security-remained-unaware-he-had-died-prosecutors-say-the-continuing-payments-ultimately-reached-109746/articleshow/134587693.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T16:07:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134588140,imgsize-1029947.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan woman allegedly took $121,000 while her disabled uncle lived without utilities]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134590191.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Over seven years, Laura Whisenant reportedly misappropriated nearly $121,000 in Social Security funds intended for her uncle, who was left without essential services. Prosecutors reveal this case is a facet of a wider crackdown by the DOJ on Social Security fraud. Numerous other cases of benefit misconduct across states have surfaced. Court proceedings are anticipated to tackle the allegations against Whisenant in the near future.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-woman-entrusted-with-managing-social-security-benefits-for-her-elderly-disabled-uncle-allegedly-took-nearly-121000-over-seven-years-while-prosecutors-say-he-lived-without-running-water-electricity-or-heat/articleshow/134590191.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-woman-entrusted-with-managing-social-security-benefits-for-her-elderly-disabled-uncle-allegedly-took-nearly-121000-over-seven-years-while-prosecutors-say-he-lived-without-running-water-electricity-or-heat/articleshow/134590191.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134590328,imgsize-1854713.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US to double EB-5 visa fees from November 30: What it means for Indian investors seeking green card]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134590844.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-to-double-eb-5-visa-fees-from-november-30-what-it-means-for-indian-investors-seeking-green-card/articleshow/134590844.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-to-double-eb-5-visa-fees-from-november-30-what-it-means-for-indian-investors-seeking-green-card/articleshow/134590844.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T16:02:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134591168,imgsize-100430.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Ethan Eriksen: 16-year-old built snow pants brand, won $5,000 prize]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134589825.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-ethan-eriksen-16-year-old-wisconsin-student-who-wanted-flame-covered-snow-pants-built-his-own-brand-and-won-a-5000-state-entrepreneur-prize/articleshow/134589825.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-ethan-eriksen-16-year-old-wisconsin-student-who-wanted-flame-covered-snow-pants-built-his-own-brand-and-won-a-5000-state-entrepreneur-prize/articleshow/134589825.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T15:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134590058,imgsize-341235.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pilot stabbed, blood in cockpit: Passengers recall harrowing ordeal on Flydubai flight that nearly crashed]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134589662.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/pilot-stabbed-blood-in-cockpit-passengers-recall-harrowing-ordeal-on-flydubai-flight-that-nearly-crashed/articleshow/134589662.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/pilot-stabbed-blood-in-cockpit-passengers-recall-harrowing-ordeal-on-flydubai-flight-that-nearly-crashed/articleshow/134589662.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T15:12:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134589914,imgsize-88822.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Flydubai flight incident: What we know about the pilot under investigation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134589697.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A flydubai flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv had to make an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia after a serious incident. Reports indicate an altercation between the pilots, leading to a rapid descent of the aircraft. Israeli fighter jets were dispatched due to concerns over a possible hijacking, which were later dismissed. Passengers reported hearing screams and witnessing a violent situation within the cockpit during the incident.]]></description><l