8-year-old-mariachi-singer-elisa-gastellum-died-before-moving-to-las-vegas-20-years-later-27-scholarships-in-her-name-have-helped-10-recipients-become-mariachi-teachers/articleshow/134583824.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2006-18-year-old-mariachi-singer-elisa-gastellum-died-before-moving-to-las-vegas-20-years-later-27-scholarships-in-her-name-have-helped-10-recipients-become-mariachi-teachers/articleshow/134583824.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134583884,imgsize-617275.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[2,100-year-old Roman shipwreck with 122 tableware types found in Turkey]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134584079.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Marine archaeologists discovered an ancient shipwreck near Adrasan, Turkey, containing thousands of ceramic tableware pieces. The cargo, believed to originate from Rhosus, dates back approximately 2,100 years. Researchers have recovered various ceramic types, revealing insights into ancient tableware and packing methods. The discovery highlights the historical significance of Rhosus in tableware production during the Late Hellenistic and Early Roman periods.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/2100-year-old-shipwreck-filled-with-122-varieties-of-ancient-roman-tableware-found-by-archaeologists-in-turkey-was-mentioned-in-a-letter-by-roman-statesman-cicero/articleshow/134584079.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/2100-year-old-shipwreck-filled-with-122-varieties-of-ancient-roman-tableware-found-by-archaeologists-in-turkey-was-mentioned-in-a-letter-by-roman-statesman-cicero/articleshow/134584079.cms]]